Q: How to scroll to the bottom of a RecyclerView? scrollToPosition doesn&#39;t work A: <p>It took me a while to figure out that if you're using Paging (that is, the adapter is a subclass of <code>PagingDataAdapter</code> then adding items is asynchronous and just calling <code>scrollToPosition</code> will not work since the items might not be loaded yet. Instead you have to get the adapater to tell you when it's updated the <code>RecyclerView</code>, eg like this</p>
<pre><code>pagingAdapter.registerAdapterDataObserver(object : RecyclerView.AdapterDataObserver() {
    override fun onItemRangeInserted(positionStart: Int, itemCount: Int) {
        (recyclerView.layoutManager as LinearLayoutManager)
            .scrollToPositionWithOffset(position, 0)
        startPostponedEnterTransition()  // &lt;- Also a good place to do this if you need it
        pagingAdapter.unregisterAdapterDataObserver(this)
    }
})
</code></pre>

Q: Maintain billboard constant size in GLSL A: <p>I worked it out. Following the source from <a href="https://github.com/tiffany352/godot-starlight" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/tiffany352/godot-starlight</a>, it turns out the solution is to multiply the square vertex by the projected point's w coordinate:</p>
<pre><code>
    // billboard position assignment (within clip space)
    vec4 billboardNDC = starPosNDC + vec4(squareVert * billboardNDC.w, 0.f, 0.f);
</code></pre>
<p>I'm not sure why this works, but I'm happy it does.</p>
